===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To make an [[estimate]] which tends toward [[exaggerate|exaggeration]].
#: {{ant|en|lowball}}
#: {{ux|en|If we '''highball''' the price, it comes out to $240. If we lowball it, it's closer to $200.}}
# {{lb|en|US|slang|possibly|dated}} To move [[quickly]]; to [[hightail]].
#* '''1959''', ''Steam's Finest Hour'', edited by David P. Morgan, Kalmbach Publishing Co. (photo caption):
#*: {{quote|en|Booster-equipped 628 '''highballs''' west at Glen Lake, Minn., back in 1947.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1960|month=October|author=P. Ransome-Wallis|title=Modern motive power of the German Federal Railway: Part Two|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=613|text=The water-level route, the whistle and the loud staccato exhaust of this great engine recalled most vividly memories of the New York Central Hudsons '''highballing''' along the Hudson River between Harmon and Albany!}}

